---
title: Proportional checks before and after protected integration
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Relevant validation with an always-present required controller check
  accDescr: Main-targeting pull requests use documentation consistency, explicit component consumer tests, or full portable regression from the complete diff. The required controller reports actual execution and failures block protected merge. After merge, main reruns the matching documentation or component scope, or selected smoke only when an earlier successful full PR run and Git relationships cover the actual tree with unchanged validation context. Otherwise main runs full regression. Native and gameplay acceptance remain separate.
  P["Main-targeting PR<br/>complete original comparison"] --> E{"Eligible editorial paths?"}
  E -- Yes --> D["Strict structure, documents<br/>governance and diagrams"]
  E -- No --> B{"One explicit component?"}
  B -- Yes --> T["Consumer and boundary tests<br/>plus viewer logic"]
  B -- No or unknown --> F["Strict full regression<br/>and viewer tests"]
  D --> C["Always-present controller<br/>selected failure blocks merge"]
  F --> C
  T --> C
  C --> M["Protected main merge"]
  M --> A{"Main validation choice"}
  A -- Editorial or component diff --> Q["Execute matching<br/>strict selected scope"]
  A -- Qualified full PR coverage --> S["Strict selected smoke<br/>and viewer tests"]
  A -- Changed context or missing proof --> R["Strict full regression<br/>and viewer tests"]
  Q --> V["Done only for verified scope<br/>report executed and unrun lanes"]
  S --> V
  R --> V
  V -. "Separate evidence" .-> N["Native behavior and gameplay<br/>require their own acceptance"]
